{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d3623673-0431-4a70-835a-f1c29dc6b369","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94a871f63f90ec09","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-19nkc8wv/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Structured resource context in rhods-operator cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the structured resource-context log convention across the rhods-operator **cloudmanager binary**: every reconciliation error log in the cloudmanager's multi-cloud infrastructure controllers carries resource identity as structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`). The cloudmanager binary is deployed on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave) and its controllers already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger via the shared reconciler pattern; this epic adds `resourceKind` and converts message-embedded identity in error paths.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Audit** all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths of the cloudmanager binary's controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine), using grep/static analysis to produce a coverage checklist of call sites embedding resource identity in message strings.\n- **Convert message-embedded identity** to structured KV pairs (`name`, `namespace`) at every audited call site in the cloudmanager binary, where present; the shared reconciler already emits `name`/`namespace` at the reconcile entry point, so the audit focus is error paths that re-embed identity in message text.\n- **Add `resourceKind`** as a structured field to all cloudmanager controller reconciliation error logs (kind is not implied by controller name for these controllers).\n- **Cluster-scoped resource handling**: the AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine CRDs are cluster-scoped — emit `name` and `resourceKind` and omit `namespace` (or set it to empty string) rather than emitting a spurious value.\n- **CI lint rule for the cloudmanager binary's code paths**: add and verify the lint rule / static-analysis check that flags any `log.Error` call in cloudmanager-binary code missing the required structured fields or embedding name/namespace in message text, enforced in CI for this epic's surfaces.\n- **Backwards-compatibility validation**: before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error; verify the log consumers used on the deployment targets (e.g., CloudWatch) ingest the new format without configuration changes; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify any text-based alert rules relying on changed message-string patterns.\n\nField naming follows camelCase (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) per the Staff Engineer / SME input, aligning with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n- Given a reconciliation error log call in the cloudmanager binary that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text in cloudmanager-binary code paths.\n- Given a cluster-scoped cloudmanager resource is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or empty — measured by a unit test confirming cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n- Given a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error before and after this epic's changes, when the log outputs are compared, then structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes — measured by a documented before/after comparison, including identification (with SRE/Support) of any text-based alert rules requiring updates.\n- The CI lint rule fails the build for any new `log.Error` call in cloudmanager-binary code paths missing the required structured fields — measured by the rule running in CI with a demonstrated failure case.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- \\[P0\\] All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n- \\[P0\\] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — cloudmanager-binary call sites.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57317,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93b89d282589a824","agent_id":"abb90b1e07d9c0812","session_id":"4f0c1725-de57-4c53-a64c-2ffcce58d254","uuid":"31b126a6-6d95-45f5-b5f1-e13a9686af04","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:35:10.639Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010 into epics"}
