ss in test logger output.\n50\t- Given a reconciliation error log call in the cloudmanager binary that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the log call uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text in cloudmanager-binary code paths.\n51\t- Given a cluster-scoped cloudmanager resource is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or empty — measured by a unit test confirming cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n52\t- Given a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error before and after this epic's changes, when the log outputs are compared, then structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes — measured by a documented before/after comparison, including identification (with SRE/Support) of any text-based alert rules requiring updates.\n53\t- The CI lint rule fails the build for any new `log.Error` call in cloudmanager-binary code paths missing the required structured fields — measured by the rule running in CI with a demonstrated failure case.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- \\[P0\\] All cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n58\t- \\[P0\\] All rhods-operator reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in message strings are converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) — cloudmanager-binary call sites.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d50220eae4577bc","agent_id":"a8b8f8b1baed9e039","session_id":"4f0c1725-de57-4c53-a64c-2ffcce58d254","uuid":"2bea461d-2140-4a23-8d80-259e2bed221e","timestamp":"2